senses.gloss:
suvacas,
(1) adj. (= Pali suvaca, subbaca; not in this sense Skt. suvaca and Lex. ˚cas), compliant, mild, gentle in speech: agrakulīnā ˚cā (mss. sucavā) tyāgarucimārdavavatī (mss. ˚tā) ca Mv 〔i.143.2〕 (vs); ˚cāḥ Mvy 〔2366〕 = Tib. bkaḥ blo bde ba, of cheerful speech;
(2) n. of a ‘gandharva maid’: Kv 〔5.18〕.

suvarṇa, m.,
(1) (= AMg. suvaṇṇa, Skt. suparṇa; cf. suvarṇin), the garuḍa bird, ‘king of birds’: suvarṇarājāno suvarṇādhipatayo (in 〔i.208.8〕 mss. suvarṇa-patayo) Mv 〔i.208.8〕; 〔212.6〕 = 〔ii.16.3〕; 〔ii.164.3—4〕; others, Mv 〔ii.91.13〕; 〔iii.83.20〕; 〔84.5〕; Mmk 〔655.8〕 (pakṣiṇāṃ rājā);
(2) n. of a former Buddha: Mv 〔i.138.6〕.

Suvarṇagarbha,
(1) n. of a Bodhisattva: Mvy 〔664〕; Suv 〔120.4〕;
(2) n. of a former Buddha: Sukh 〔6.13〕.

Suvarṇaprabha,
(1) n. of a former Buddha: Sukh 〔5.13〕;
(2) n. of a Māra: Gv 〔444.12〕.

Suvarṇabhāsottama,
(1) also -sūtra, n. of a work (our Suv); this form preferred by Nobel, 〔p. xii〕, tho most Nep. mss. read usually Suvarṇaprabhās˚; in vss also Svarṇa˚ occurs for Suvarṇa˚; and sometimes, when modifying deśanā, the name becomes ˚ttamā, f.: Suv 〔2.1〕 (vs; Svarṇa˚); 〔13.8〕; 〔14.2〕; 〔28.12〕 and 〔29.1〕 (vss; Svarṇa- ˚ttamā, with deśanā); etc. Note also Svarṇaprabhāsa Suv 〔53.18〕 (vs);
(2) m., n. of a Bodhisattva: Suv 〔120.3〕 (most mss. Suvarṇaprabhās˚).

Suvikrāntavikrāmin,
(1) (v.l. ˚kramin, ˚krama) n. of a satpurusa, q.v.: SP 〔4.1〕;
(2) n. of a work: Mvy 〔1347〕 (˚mī, n. sg. m.);
(3) n. of a Bodhisattva: ŚsP 〔6.17〕.

Suviśuddha,
(1) n. of a former Buddha: Mv 〔i.139.7〕;
(2) m. or (˚dhā) f., n. of a lokadhātu: SP 〔205.8〕 (vs; ˚dha n. sg., could be for ˚dhā m.c.).
